intro='''<header class="top"><a class="brand" href="#top">AGENTIC ATLAS Q&A</a><span class="edition">A practical study document · Edition 02</span><button id="mobile-nav" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="contents">Categories</button></header><div class="layout"><nav class="sidebar" id="contents" aria-label="Categories"><h2>Explore the categories</h2>NAV</nav><main id="top"><div class="eyebrow">THE BUILDER’S STUDY GUIDE</div><h1>Agentic Atlas <span>Q&A</span></h1><p class="intro">Understand the concepts. Explain the tradeoffs. Build systems that work. A categorized reference for interviews, project planning, and everyday engineering decisions.</p><div class="stats"><div class="stat"><strong>__CATEGORIES__</strong><span>Categories</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>__QUESTIONS__</strong><span>Answered questions</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>__TOPICS__</strong><span>Topics · each with 3 levels</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>Offline</strong><span>One self-contained file</span></div></div><aside class="scope"><p><strong>What this edition covers.</strong> All 72 questions visible in your supplied carousel images, plus __ADDITIONS__ clearly labeled additions. The original 100 answers are retained and expanded into __CATEGORIES__ categories and __TOPICS__ topics. Every topic has Basic, Intermediate, and Advanced questions with answers.</p><p>The images credit <strong>bhavs.ai</strong> and advertise a 223-question PDF. That PDF was not supplied; this document does not reproduce or claim access to its unseen questions or answers. Answers here are newly written. The taxonomy is a broad learning map, not a claim that the field has a fixed or exhaustive set of categories.</p><p><strong>Study tip:</strong> choose one category, explain an answer out loud, then compare it with the reference. Behavioral answers are preparation frameworks, not claims about your personal experience.</p></aside><div class="toolbar" role="search"><label class="search"><span class="sr-only">Search questions, answers and topics</span><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search a question, concept, or tradeoff…" autocomplete="off"></label><label class="filter"><span class="sr-only">Difficulty</span><select id="level"><option value="all">All levels</option><option>Basic</option><option>Intermediate</option><option>Advanced</option></select></label><label class="filter"><span class="sr-only">Question source</span><select id="origin"><option value="all">All questions</option><option value="Provided images">From your images</option><option value="Added topic">Added questions</option></select></label></div><div class="browse-filters"><label class="filter"><span class="sr-only">Filter by category</span><select id="category-filter"><option value="all">All categories</option>__CATEGORY_OPTIONS__</select></label><label class="filter"><span class="sr-only">Filter by topic</span><select id="topic-filter"><option value="all">All topics</option>__TOPIC_OPTIONS__</select></label></div><div class="actions"><button id="expand">Expand visible answers</button><button id="collapse">Collapse answers</button><button id="practice" class="primary">Practice a question</button><button id="print">Print / Save PDF</button><button id="reset">Reset filters</button></div><p id="count" class="result-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">__QUESTIONS__ questions available</p><section class="study-box" id="study" hidden aria-labelledby="practice-title"><h2 id="practice-title">Practice out loud</h2><p id="study-meta"></p><p class="study-prompt" id="study-question"></p><button id="reveal">Reveal reference answer</button><button id="next">Another question</button><button id="close-study">Close practice</button><div class="study-answer" id="study-answer" hidden></div></section><p class="empty" id="empty" hidden>No matching questions. Try a broader term or reset the filters.</p><noscript><p class="scope">JavaScript is disabled. All questions and answers remain available: open each answer using its heading. Search, filters, and practice require JavaScript.</p></noscript>'''.replace('NAV',''.join(nav))
